 39:25 in P often (12 t.) of the divinE presence, or dwelling, in the midst of Israel, Exod 25:8 ; Exod 29:45 ; Exod 29:46 ; Lev 15:31 ; Lev 16:16 + (Carpenter Hex. i. 209, ed. 2, 410 ; J E D in such cases have always קֶרֶב ), so Ezek 37:26 ; Ezek 37:28 ; Ezek 43:7 ; Ezek 43:9 , compare Hag 2:5 מִן , as Gen 19:29 מִתּוֺךְ הַהֲפֵכָה , Exod 3:2 ׳ מִתּ הַסְּנֶה , Exod 33:11 הָאֹהֶל ׳ לאֹ יָמִישׁ מִתּ , Deut 4:12 + הָאֵשׁ ׳ מִתּ , 1Sam 15:6 עֲמָלֵק ׳ רְדוּ מִתּ ; = from among , as to take, separate, etc., מִתּוֺכָם , הָעָם ׳ מִתּ , etc., Exod 7:5 ; Exod 28:1 ; Num 3:12 ; Num 4:2 ; Num 4:18 ; Num 16:21 ; Num 16:33 ; Num 17:10 ; Num 19:20 (all P ) +; אֶל , as Exod 14:23 ויבאואֶ֗֗֗לאתּוֺךְ הַיָּם , Lev 11:33 ; Num 17:12 וַיָּרָץ הַקָּהָל ׳ אֶלאתּ , Num 19:6 ; Deut 21:12 בֵּיתֶ֫ךָ ׳ וַהֲבֵאתָהּ אֶלאתּ , Deut 22:2 ; Deut 23:11 ; 2Sam 3:27 ; 2Sam 4:6 ; Jer 21:4 +; מֵעַל Ezek 11:23 . — תוך is used by most writers, occurring approximately 8-10 times in many books, but is especially frequent in P (c. 106 t,) and Ezekiel (116 t.). synonym קֶרֶב , q. v.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9124')\">BDB9124</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8432')\">H8432</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9123')\">BDB9123</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9125')\">BDB9125</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>תָּ֫וֶךְ</bdbheb><sub>418</sub> <b>substantive</b> <highlightword>midst</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, also denominative <bdbheb>תִּוֵּוךְ</bdbheb>; √ unknown; not apparently in cognate languages); — absolute <bdbheb>תָּ֫וֶךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 15:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,10)\">Gen 15:10</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>תּוֺךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 1:6\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(1,1,6)\">Gen 1:6</ref> +; <bdbheb>תּוֺכִי</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>תּוֺכוֺ</bdbheb>, etc., 2 feminine singular <bdbheb>תּוֺכֵּ֫ כִי</bdbheb> <r